---
title: Apple Crisp
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Desserts
cook time: 30-40 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@sliced apples{5-6}
@flour{1%cup}
@sugar{1/2 to 1%cup} (depending on tartness of apples)
@baking powder{1%tsp}
@salt{3/4%tsp}
@unbeaten egg{1}
@cinnamon{0.5%tsp}
@butter, melted and cooled{1/3%cup}

Place apples into a greased 6x10 inch baking dish. Mix flour, sugar, baking powder, salt and unbeaten egg until crumbly. Sprinkle over apples. Pour cooled butter over top. Sprinkle with cinnamon. Bake for 30-40 minutes at 350 degrees. Serve warm as is, or top with whipped cream, ice cream or cream.
